Precompute for single coset: g^(coset_idx + 1)\n    Fp const g_coset = pow(g_shift, coset_idx + 1);\n    \n    // Intermediate buffer layout for coset-parallel:\n    // [buffer_size][num_cosets * num_threads_per_coset]\n    uint32_t global_tidx = coset_idx * gridDim.x * blockDim.x + tidx;\n    inter_buffer = d_intermediates + global_tidx;\n    buffer_stride = gridDim.x * gridDim.y * blockDim.x;\n    \n    // Use NUM_COSETS=1 context for single coset\n    NttEvalContext<1> eval_ctx{ /* ... */ };\n    \n    // ... processing loop ...\n    \n    // Output layout: [num_blocks][num_cosets * skip_domain]\n    tmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * num_cosets * skip_domain + coset_idx * skip_domain + ntt_idx] =\n        tile_sum;\n}\n```\n\n**Comments from source (Lines 331-333):**\n```\n// Coset-parallel kernel: grid.y = num_cosets, each block handles ONE coset.\n// Uses acc_constraints<1, NEEDS_SHMEM> with explicit parameter passing.\n// Use when num_x * skip_domain is small for better GPU utilization.\n```\n\n**Threshold for Mode Selection (Line 27):**\n```cpp\nconstexpr uint32_t COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768; // 2^15\n```\n\nWhen `num_x * skip_domain < 32768`, the kernel uses coset-parallel mode with `grid.y = num_cosets`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Key Optimization Insights:\n\n1. **NttEvalContext** enables efficient lockstep evaluation by precomputing `omega_shifts` for all cosets and reusing the coefficient across the iNTT operation.\n\n2. **Batched Degenerate Kernel** uses per-window metadata to avoid redundant computation in independent processing units, improving occupancy.\n\n3. **Coset-Parallel Mode** trades redundant NTT operations for better GPU utilization when the problem size is small (grid.y = num_cosets).\n\n4. **Grid Dimension Strategy:**\n   - Lockstep: 1D grid `(num_x_blocks, 1)`\n   - Coset-parallel: 2D grid `(num_x_blocks, num_cosets)`\n\n5. **Buffer Layouts:**\n   - Lockstep intermediates: `[buffer_size][num_threads][NUM_COSETS]`\n   - Coset-parallel interm