es:\n\n```cpp\ntemplate <bool COSET_PARALLEL>\ninline std::pair<dim3, dim3> eval_constraints_launch_params(\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t num_cosets,\n    size_t max_temp_bytes,\n    uint32_t buffer_threshold,\n    uint32_t max_threads_per_block\n) {\n    // ASSERTION: full skip domain must fit in one block\n    assert(skip_domain <= 1024 && \"skip_domain exceeds CUDA max threads per block (1024)\");\n    auto max_threads = std::max(skip_domain, max_threads_per_block);\n    auto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(skip_domain * num_x, max_threads);\n\n    if constexpr (COSET_PARALLEL) {\n        grid.y = num_cosets; // 2D grid for coset-parallel mode\n    }\n    // grid.y = 1 implicitly for lockstep mode\n\n    // Buffer size calculation (same for both modes)\n    size_t desired_intermed_capacity_bytes =\n        buffer_size <= buffer_threshold\n            ? 0\n            : (size_t)grid.x * block.x * num_cosets * buffer_size * sizeof(Fp);\n\n    uint32_t num_x_per_thread = std::max(\n        div_ceil(desired_intermed_capacity_bytes, std::max(max_temp_bytes, (size_t)1)), (size_t)1\n    );\n    if (num_x_per_thread <= grid.x) {\n        grid.x = grid.x / num_x_per_thread;\n    } else {\n        grid.x = 1;\n        block.x = std::max(num_x / num_x_per_thread, 1u) * skip_domain;\n    }\n\n    return {grid, block};\n}\n```\n\n**temp_sums_buffer_size (Lines 60-81):**\n```cpp\n// Output layout: [num_blocks][num_cosets * skip_domain]\nreturn grid.x * num_cosets * skip_domain;\n```\n\n**intermediates_buffer_size (Lines 84-107):**\n```cpp\n// Layout: [buffer_size][num_threads][num_cosets]\nreturn grid.x * block.x * buffer_size * num_cosets;\n```\n\n---\n\n**coset_round0_config Namespace (Lines 112-134):**\n\nLockstep mode wrapper that calls the shared implementation with `COSET_PARALLEL=false`:\n\n```cpp\ninline std::pair<dim3, dim3> eval_constraints_launch_params(\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t num_cosets,\n    size_t max_temp_bytes,\n    uint32_t buffer_threshold,\n    uint32_t max_threads_per_block\n) {\n    return round0_config_impl::eval_constraints_launch_params<false>(\n        buffer_size,\n        skip_domain,\n        num_x,\n        num_cosets,\n        max_temp_bytes,\n        buffer_threshold,\n        max_threads_per_block\n    );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n**coset_parallel_round0_config Namespace (Lines 138-160):**\n\nCoset-parallel mode wrapper that calls the shared implementation with `COSET_PARALLEL=true`:\n\n```cpp\ninline std::pair<dim3, dim3> eval_constraints_launch_params(\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t num_cosets,\n    size_t max_temp_bytes,\n    uint32_t buffer_threshold,\n    uint32_t max_threads_per_block\n) {\n    return round0_config_impl::eval_constraints_launch_params<true>(\n        buffer_size,\n        skip_domain,\n        num_x,\n        num_cosets,\n        max_temp_bytes,\n        buffer_threshold,\n        max_threads_per_block\n    );\n}\n```\n\n**Key Difference:**\n- **Lockstep mode:** `grid.y = 1` (implicitly), each thread handles all `num_cosets`\n- **Coset-parallel mode:** `grid.y = num_cosets`, each block handles one coset identified by `blockIdx.y`\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Coset-Parallel Kernel Usage Example**\n\n**File Path:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n\n**Coset-Parallel Kernel Definition (Lines 334-467):**\n\nKey structural pattern:\n```cpp\n__global__ void zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel(\n    // ... parameters ...\n) {\n    // ... setup code ...\n    \n    uint32_t const coset_idx = blockIdx.y;  // KEY: coset selected by grid dimension y\n    \n    // Precompute for single coset: g^(coset_idx + 1)\n    Fp const g_coset = pow(g_shift, coset_idx + 1);\n    \n    // Intermediate buffer layout for coset-parallel:\n    // [buffer_size][num_cosets * num_threads_per_coset]\n    uint32_t global_tidx = coset_idx * gridDim.x * blockDim.x + tidx;\n    inter_buffer = d_intermediates + global_tidx;\n    buffer_stride = gridDim.x * gridDim.y * blockDim.x;\n    \n    // Use NUM_COSETS=1 context for single coset\n    NttEvalContext<1> eval_ctx{ /* ... */ };\n    \n    // ... processing loop ...\n    \n    // Output layout: [num_blocks][num_cosets * skip_domain]\n    tmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * num_cosets * skip_domain + coset_idx * skip_domain + ntt_idx] =\n        tile_sum;\n}\n```\n\n**Comments from source (Lines 331-333):**\n```\n// Coset-parallel kernel: grid.y = num_cosets, each block handles ONE coset.\n// Uses acc_constraints<1, NEEDS_SHMEM> with explicit parameter passing.\n// Use when num_x * skip_domain is small for better GPU utilization.\n```\n\n**Threshold for Mode Selection (Line 27):**\n```cpp\nconstexpr uint32_t COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768; // 2^15\n```\n\nWhen `num_x * skip_domain < 32768`, the kernel uses coset-parallel mode with `grid.y = num_cosets`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Key Optimization Insights:\n\n1. **NttEvalContext** enables efficient lockstep evaluation by precomputing `omega_shifts` for all cosets and reusing the coefficient across the iNTT operation.\n\n2. **Batched Degenerate Kernel** uses per-window metadata to avoid redundant computation in independent processing units, improving occupancy.\n\n3. **Coset-Parallel Mode** trades redundant NTT operations for better GPU utilization when the problem size is small (grid.y = num_cosets).\n\n4. **Grid Dimension Strategy:**\n   - Lockstep: 1D grid `(num_x_blocks, 1)`\n   - Coset-parallel: 2D grid `(num_x_blocks, num_cosets)`\n\n5. **Buffer Layouts:**\n   - Lockstep intermediates: `[buffer_size][num_threads][NUM_COSETS]`\n   - Coset-parallel intermediates: `[buffer_size][num_cosets * num_threads_per_coset]`"}],"totalDurationMs":72598,"totalTokens":60041,"totalToolUseCount":26,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1