{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012TiSHWAPeHtSfM2cmShzFQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Comprehensive Report: Batched Degenerate Stacked Reduction Optimization\n\nBased on commit 6fccffce, here is the complete pattern for the batched degenerate stacked reduction optimization:\n\n### 1. METADATA STRUCTURE\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (lines 159-171)\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\npub(crate) struct DegenerateWindowMeta {\n    col_offset: u32,           // Offset into unstacked_cols array\n    eq_ub_offset: u32,         // Offset into eq_ub_all (concatenated values)\n    window_len: u32,           // Number of columns in this window\n    _pad: u32,                 // Padding for alignment\n    eq_r: EF,                  // Stable eq evaluation (16 bytes, 4 x 32-bit fields)\n    k_rot_r: EF,               // Stable k_rot evaluation (16 bytes)\n}\n// Total: 48 bytes (exact match with CUDA-side layout)\n```\n\n**CUDA definition (matching Rust layout):** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (lines 36-43)\n\nThe per-window metadata encapsulates all the information needed for a block to independently compute its contribution without accessing main orchestration structures.\n\n### 2. CUDA KERNEL: GRID ORGANIZATION AND COMPUTATION\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (lines 379-448)\n\n**Kernel signature:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel(\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_ub_all,\n    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_global,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_global,\n    const DegenerateWindowMeta *__restrict__ metas,\n    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t shift_factor\n)\n```\n\n**Grid Layout:**\n- **Grid dimensions:** `dim3(num_windows, 1, 1)` — one block per degenerate window\n  - Each `blockIdx.x` corresponds to a window index\n  - No use of `blockIdx.y` or `blockIdx.z` (though the pattern is extensible)\n- **Block size:** `dim3(256, 1, 1)` — 256 threads per block (full warp-aligned blocks)\n- **Shared memory:** `div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt)` = 32 FpExt entries for reduction\n\n**Computation pattern per block:**\n\n1. **Block-level metadata load** (line 394): `DegenerateWindowMeta meta = metas[blockIdx.x]`\n   - Loads pre-computed `eq_r` and `k_rot_r` for this window\n   - Computes pointers into the global arrays:\n     - `unstacked_cols = unstacked_cols_global + meta.col_offset`\n     - `lambda_pows = lambda_pows_global + 2 * meta.col_offset`\n     - `eq_ub_ptr = eq_ub_all + meta.eq_ub_offset`\n\n2. **Thread-level iteration** (line 408): Each thread processes a slice of the window\n   ```cuda\n   for (uint32_t window_idx = threadIdx.x; window_idx < window_len; window_idx += blockDim.x)\n   ```\n   - Threads cooperatively iterate over the window in strides of block size\n   - No synchronization overhead for inter-window coordination\n\n3. **Per-element computation** (lines 409-438):\n   - Extract `UnstackedSlice` metadata for this entry\n   - Fetch polynomial evaluations `q_0, q_1` from the appropriate commit index\n   - Compute linear interpolation: `q_x = q_0 + q_c1 * x` for x ∈ {1, 2} (S_DEG=2)\n   - For each x value, compute:\n     - `eq_ub_x = eq_ub * eq1(x, b)` (eq1 is the bivariate equality polynomial on {0,1}²)\n     - Combined eq: `eq = eq_r * eq_ub_x`\n     - Combined k_rot: `k_rot = k_rot_r * eq_ub_x`\n   - Accumulate: `local_sums[x] += (lambda[2*window_idx] * eq + lambda[2*window_idx+1] * k_rot) * q_x`\n\n4. **Block-level reduction** (lines 440-447):\n   - For each of the S_DEG=2 outputs:\n     ```cuda\n     FpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(local_sums[idx], shared);\n     if (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n         sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced);\n     }\n     ```\n   - `block_reduce_sum`: Two-stage reduction (warp-level via `__shfl_down_sync`, then inter-warp via shared memory)\n   - Result is accumulated atomically into global output buffer at offset `idx * 4` (4 u64 values per FpExt)\n\n**Output buffer format:**\n- Single global `uint64_t *output` of size `[STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG * D_EF]` = `[2 * 4]` = 8 u64 values\n- All blocks atomically add their contributions to the same output buffer\n- Layout: `[EF[0].elem[0..3], EF[1].elem[0..3]]` (4 u64 per FpExt, 2 FpExt outputs)\n\n**Launch wrapper** (lines 652-675):\n```cuda\nextern \"C\" int _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    const FpExt *const *q_evals,\n    const FpExt *eq_ub_all,\n    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols,\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows,\n    const DegenerateWindowMeta *metas,\n    uint64_t *output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t num_windows,\n    uint32_t shift_factor\n) {\n    dim3 block(256);\n    dim3 grid(num_windows);\n    size_t shmem_bytes = div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt);\n    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(...);\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n### 3. RUST-SIDE ORCHESTRATION: METADATA COLLECTION AND BATCHED LAUNCH\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (lines 846-912)\n\nThe orchestration follows a 3-phase strategy:\n\n**Phase 1: Window Classification & Metadata Collection** (lines 846-871)\n\n```rust\nlet mut degen_metas: Vec<DegenerateWindowMeta> = Vec::new();\nlet mut degen_eq_ub: Vec<EF> = Vec::new();\nlet mut non_degen_windows: Vec<[usize; 2]> = Vec::new();\n\nfor window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2) {\n    let window_start = window[0];\n    let window_end = window[1];\n    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_height as usize;\n\n    if log_height < l_skip + round {  // Degenerate case\n        let eq_ub_offset = degen_eq_ub.len();\n        degen_eq_ub.extend_from_slice(&self.eq_ub_per_trace[window_start..window_end]);\n        degen_metas.push(DegenerateWindowMeta {\n            col_offset: window_start as u32,\n            eq_ub_offset: eq_ub_offset as u32,\n            window_len: window_len as u32,\n            _pad: 0,\n            eq_r: self.eq_stable[log_height],\n            k_rot_r: self.k_rot_stable[log_height],\n        });\n    } else {  // Non-degenerate: process individually later\n        non_degen_windows.push([window_start, window_end]);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Key operations:**\n- **Classification criterion:** `log_height < l_skip + round` determines degeneracy\n- **Metadata accumulation:** Build up `DegenerateWindowMeta` structs with:\n  - `col_offset`: Direct indices into the unstacked columns array (no need to copy)\n  - `eq_ub_offset`: Tracked offset into a concatenated buffer (to enable single H2D transfer)\n  - Pre-computed `eq_r` and `k_rot_r` lookups from stability tables\n- **eq_ub concatenation:** All per-window eq_ub values packed sequentially (1 per unstacked column)\n\n**Phase 2: Batched Launch** (lines 876-912)\n\n```rust\nif !degen_metas.is_empty() {\n    // Zero-initialize accumulator (reused across all windows)\n    self.d_accum.fill_zero()?;\n    \n    // Upload metadata array\n    let d_metas = degen_metas.to_device()?;\n    \n    // Upload concatenated eq_ub values\n    if degen_eq_ub.len() > self.d_eq_ub.len() {\n        self.d_eq_ub = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(degen_eq_ub.len());\n    }\n    degen_eq_ub.copy_to(&mut self.d_eq_ub)?;\n    \n    // Single kernel launch for all degenerate windows\n    let stacked_height = self.stacked_height(round);\n    unsafe {\n        stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n            &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n            &self.d_eq_ub,\n            &self.d_unstacked_cols,\n            &self.d_lambda_pows,\n            &d_metas,\n            &mut self.d_accum,\n            stacked_height,\n            degen_metas.len(),\n            l_skip,\n            round,\n        )?;\n    }\n    \n    // D2H copy and atomic reduction to final format\n    let h_accum = self.d_accum.to_host()?;\n    let degen_evals = reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum);\n    for i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n        total_evals[i] += degen_evals[i];\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Upload pattern:**\n- **d_metas**: Temporary device buffer (metadata is small, ~48 bytes per window)\n- **d_eq_ub**: Reusable persistent buffer, sized to hold the largest concatenated eq_ub batch\n- **d_unstacked_cols, d_lambda_pows**: Pre-existing global device buffers (no copies needed)\n\n**Atomic reduction on GPU:**\n- All blocks accumulate into a single 8 u64 buffer (`STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG * D_EF`)\n- Device atomics handle race-free accumulation\n\n**Host-side finalization** (`reduce_raw_u64_to_ef`, `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/utils.rs:40`):\n```rust\npub fn reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(accum: &[u64]) -> Vec<EF> {\n    accum\n        .chunks_exact(D_EF)  // D_EF = 4 (BabyBear extension degree)\n        .map(|chunk| {\n            EF::from_basis_coefficients_fn(|i| {\n                let monty_raw = (chunk[i] % F::ORDER_U64) as u32;\n                unsafe { transmute::<u32, F>(monty_raw) }\n            })\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n```\n- Interprets each block of 4 u64 values as a single field element (in Montgomery form)\n- Takes modulo `F::ORDER_U64` to handle overflow from atomic additions\n- Converts back to field representation\n\n**Phase 3: Non-Degenerate Windows** (lines 914-949)\n\nIndividual per-window launches continue using the existing `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round` kernel with per-window `eq_r_ns` and `k_rot_ns` arrays. Each accumulates into a zero-initialized `d_accum`, D2H transfers, and partial-sum collection.\n\nFinal result is aggregated:\n```rust\nfor i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n    total_evals[i] += degen_evals[i];\n    total_evals[i] += non_degen_evals[i];\n}\n```\n\n### 4. PERFORMANCE IMPACT\n\n**Measured at APC 300 (Additive Polynomial Code parameter set):**\n- **Before:** ~10,348 individual degenerate kernel launches (each with fill_zero + H2D + kernel + D2H + modular reduction overhead)\n- **After:** 1 batched kernel launch per round\n- **Stacked Reduction time:** 312ms → 147ms (2.12× improvement)\n- **Overall STARK excl trace time:** 2370ms → 2195ms (1.08× improvement)\n- **Scaling ratio improvement:** 1.088 → 1.022 (indicating more balanced compute distribution)\n\n### 5. TEMPLATE FOR ROUND 0 BATCHING OPTIMIZATION\n\nTo apply a similar pattern to Round 0 (SP_DEG=1, outputs G0/G1/G2):\n\n1. **Define Round0Meta struct:**\n   ```rust\n   #[repr(C)]\n   pub struct Round0WindowMeta {\n       col_offset: u32,\n       window_len: u32,\n       _pad: u64,  // padding to align larger fields\n       // If needed, pre-computed coefficients\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **Create batched kernel variant:**\n   - Grid: `dim3(num_windows, 1, 1)` (one block per window)\n   - Block: `dim3(256 or 512, 1, 1)` (tune for latency)\n   - Shared memory: For block reduction of NUM_G=3 outputs\n   - Output buffer: Single global `uint64_t[NUM_G * D_EF]` with atomic accumulation\n\n3. **Orchestration (same 3-phase pattern):**\n   - Classify windows by degenerate/non-degenerate criteria (if applicable)\n   - Collect metadata into vectors\n   - Upload metadata & concatenated data\n   - Single kernel launch with all blocks\n   - D2H copy + `reduce_raw_u64_to_ef` for each output\n\n4. **Key differences from degenerate case:**\n   - Round 0 has 3 outputs (NUM_G=3) instead of 2 (S_DEG=2)\n   - May not have a degeneracy classification (all Round 0 windows always batch)\n   - Grid should use `gridDim.x` for window index; if scaling beyond 65535 windows, may need `gridDim.y` for secondary batching (careful with atomic contention)\n\n---\n\n**File locations for reference:**\n- CUDA kernel definition: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (lines 36–43, 379–448, 652–675)\n- Rust metadata struct: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (lines 159–171)\n- Rust FFI wrapper: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` (lines 80–90, 291–316)\n- Rust orchestration: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (lines 846–912)\n- Atomic reduction helpers: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/include/sumcheck.cuh` (line 160+)\n- Host-side finalization: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/utils.rs` (line 40)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db10821c-17ee-4d4a-acd4-fd3a20fcece6","uuid":"b4710756-d5d1-434b-98bc-d718928ed598","timestamp":"2026-04-10T18:54:58.205Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /home/georg/stark-backend, I need to understand the recently-implemented \"batched degenerate stacked reduction\" optimization. This was committed as \"perf: batch degenerate stacked reduction kernel launches\" (commit 6fccffce).\n\n1. Look at the git diff for commit 6fccffce to understand what was changed.\n2. Find and read the batched kernel in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction/` — look for kernels with \"batched\" or \"batch\" in the name, and any per-AIR metadata struct.\n3. Find the Rust-side orchestration that collects metadata and does the batched launch — look in `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction/` for the code that builds metadata arrays and issues batched launches.\n\nReport the full pattern: metadata struct, how grid dimensions use blockIdx.z, how the Rust side collects per-AIR info and uploads it, and how the final reduction works. This will serve as the template for a similar Round 0 batching optimization.","agentId":