t_factor\n)\n```\n\n**Grid Layout:**\n- **Grid dimensions:** `dim3(num_windows, 1, 1)` — one block per degenerate window\n  - Each `blockIdx.x` corresponds to a window index\n  - No use of `blockIdx.y` or `blockIdx.z` (though the pattern is extensible)\n- **Block size:** `dim3(256, 1, 1)` — 256 threads per block (full warp-aligned blocks)\n- **Shared memory:** `div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt)` = 32 FpExt entries for reduction\n\n**Computation pattern per block:**\n\n1. **Block-level metadata load** (line 394): `DegenerateWindowMeta meta = metas[blockIdx.x]`\n   - Loads pre-computed `eq_r` and `k_rot_r` for this window\n   - Computes pointers into the global arrays:\n     - `unstacked_cols = unstacked_cols_global + meta.col_offset`\n     - `lambda_pows = lambda_pows_global + 2 * meta.col_offset`\n     - `eq_ub_ptr = eq_ub_all + meta.eq_ub_offset`\n\n2. **Thread-level iteration** (line 408): Each thread processes a slice of the window\n   ```cuda\n   for (uint32_t window_idx = threadIdx.x; window_idx < window_len; window_idx += blockDim.x)\n   ```\n   - Threads cooperatively iterate over the window in strides of block size\n   - No synchronization overhead for inter-window coordination\n\n3. **Per-element computation** (lines 409-438):\n   - Extract `UnstackedSlice` metadata for this entry\n   - Fetch polynomial evaluations `q_0, q_1` from the appropriate commit index\n   - Compute linear interpolation: `q_x = q_0 + q_c1 * x` for x ∈ {1, 2} (S_DEG=2)\n   - For each x value, compute:\n     - `eq_ub_x = eq_ub * eq1(x, b)` (eq1 is the bivariate equality polynomial on {0,1}²)\n     - Combined eq: `eq = eq_r * eq_ub_x`\n     - Combined k_rot: `k_rot = k_rot_r * eq_ub_x`\n   - Accumulate: `local_sums[x] += (lambda[2*window_idx] * eq + lambda[2*window_idx+1] * k_rot) * q_x`\n\n4. **Block-level reduction** (lines 440-447):\n   - For each of the S_DEG=2 outputs:\n     ```cuda\n     FpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(local_sums[idx], shared);\n     if (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n         sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced);\n     }\n     ```\n   - `block_reduce_sum`: Two-stage reduction (warp-level via `__shfl_down_sync`, then inter-warp via shared memory)\n   - Result is accumulated atomically into global output buffer at offset `idx * 4` (4 u64 values per FpExt)\n\n**Output buffer format:**\n- Single global `uint64_t *output` of size `[STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG * D_EF]` = `[2 * 4]` = 8 u64 values\n- All blocks atomically add their contributions to the same output buffer\n- Layout: `[EF[0].elem[0..3], EF[1].elem[0..3]]` (4 u64 per FpExt, 2 FpExt outputs)\n\n**Launch wrapper** (lines 652-675):\n```cuda\nextern \"C\" int _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    const FpExt *const *q_evals,\n    const FpExt *eq_ub_all,\n    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols,\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows,\n    const DegenerateWindowMeta *metas,\n    uint64_t *output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t num_windows,\n    uint32_t shift_factor\n) {\n    dim3 block(256);\n    dim3 grid(num_windows);\n    size_t shmem_bytes = div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt);\n    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(...);\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n### 3. RUST-SIDE ORCHESTRATION: METADATA COLLECTION AND BATCHED LAUNCH\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (lines 846-912)\n\nThe orchestration follows a 3-phase strategy:\n\n**Phase 1: Window Classification & Metadata Collection** (lines 846-871)\n\n```rust\nlet mut degen_metas: Vec<DegenerateWindowMeta> = Vec::new();\nlet mut degen_eq_ub: Vec<EF> = Vec::new();\nlet mut non_degen_windows: Vec<[usize; 2]> = Vec::new();\n\nfor window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2) {\n    let window_start = window[0];\n    let window_end = window[1];\n    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_h