uffer layout compatible with batched_final_reduce_block_sums?\n4. Does the plan handle ALL the data dependencies correctly (what needs to stay alive, what can be dropped)?\n5. Are there any hidden interactions between the zerocheck and logup batches (ordering, shared state)?\n6. Is the GLOBAL=false restriction well-justified? How many AIRs might be excluded?\n7. Is the Rust-side classification logic correct (when to batch vs not)?\n\nReturn your response in exactly this format:\n\n## Findings\n(ordered by severity, with file references)\n\n## Improvements I would consider\n(real alternatives that could better improve proof time)\n\n## Assessment\n(state whether there are remaining design-level blockers, whether the plan is prototype-ready, and what the strongest part is)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_read_input_tokens":131545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db10821c-17ee-4d4a-acd4-fd3a20fcece6","uuid":"97499bdc-44fc-4d86-ab39-58cefbd296f3"}
