{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R378XDhqB3ZnSormGsMseB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch Round 0 Coset-Parallel Kernel Launches\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce Round 0 GPU time at APC 300 by batching ~935 sequential coset-parallel kernel launches into 2 batched launches (one for zerocheck, one for logup). Currently each small AIR launches its own kernel with 3-12 thread blocks on a GPU with 108+ SMs, resulting in 3-11% SM utilization per launch. Batching executes all small AIRs simultaneously in a single kernel, targeting near-100% SM utilization.\n6\t\n7\tPrimary target: Round 0 APC 300 wall time < 400ms (currently 570ms).\n8\tSecondary target: STARK excl trace APC 300 < 2050ms (currently 2205ms).\n9\t\n10\t## Current Code Path\n11\t\n12\t### Rust orchestration\n13\t\n14\t`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:599-928`) runs in two phases:\n15\t\n16\t- **Phase 1** (lines 744-841): Iterates all AIR instances sequentially. For each AIR:\n17\t  1. Builds `d_main_parts` (device array of trace column pointers) — line 781-786\n18\t  2. Calls `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` (zerocheck) — line 795-808\n19\t  3. Calls `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (logup) — line 812-827\n20\t  4. Stores `DeviceBuffer` results in `Round0Pending` vec — line 830-841\n21\t- **Phase 2** (lines 844-924): `current_stream_sync()`, then D2H + polynomial construction per AIR.\n22\t\n23\t### Per-AIR zerocheck path\n24\t\n25\t`evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` (`round0.rs:31-124`):\n26\t1. Early-returns if no constraints or `num_cosets == 0`\n27\t2. Reads pre-built rules from `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner` (d_rules, d_used_nodes, buffer_size)\n28\t3. Computes intermediates and temp_sums buffer sizes via FFI (`_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size`)\n29\t4. Allocates `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `sp_evals` on device\n30\t5. Calls FFI `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` → `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` (zerocheck_round0.cu:667-717)\n31\t\n32\tThe C dispatcher checks `use_coset_parallel_mode(num_x, skip_domain)` (threshold: `num_x * skip_domain < 32768`):\n33\t- Small AIRs → `launch_zerocheck_coset_parallel` with grid `(x_blocks, num_cosets)` — each block handles ONE coset\n34\t- Large AIRs → `dispatch_zerocheck` with lockstep kernel — each thread handles ALL cosets\n35\t\n36\tEach launcher issues 2 GPU kernel launches: evaluation kernel + `final_reduce_block_sums`.\n37\t\n38\t### Per-AIR logup path\n39\t\n40\t`evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (`round0.rs:132-275`):\n41\t1. Early-returns if no interactions (`eq_3bs.is_empty()`)\n42\t2. **Per-AIR CPU work**: Builds symbolic DAG from `symbolic.interactions`, compiles to `SymbolicRulesGpu`, computes `numer_weights` and `denom_weights`, computes `denom_sum_init`\n43\t3. Uploads `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to device (per-AIR H2D)\n44\t4. Allocates intermediates, temp_sums, output buffers\n45\t5. Calls FFI `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` → `_logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0` (logup_round0.cu:658-810)\n46\t\n47\tSame coset-parallel dispatch as zerocheck, same 2-kernel launch pattern.\n48\t\n49\t### Bottleneck summary\n50\t\n51\tAt APC 300: ~539 zerocheck + ~396 logup coset-parallel launches = ~935 evaluation kernels + ~935 reductions = **~1870 sequential GPU kernel launches**, each using 3-11% of SMs. Total coset-parallel GPU time: ~464ms (81% of Round 0's 570ms wall time).\n52\t\n53\t## Changes\n54\t\n55\t### Change 1: CUDA — Metadata structs\n56\t\n57\t**File: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`**\n58\t\n59\tAdd in the `zerocheck_round0` namespace:\n60\t\n61\t```cpp\n62\tstruct ZerocheckBatchMeta {\n63\t    const Fp *selectors_cube;          // [3][num_x]\n64\t    const Fp *preprocessed;            // per-AIR, may be null\n65\t    const Fp *const *main_parts;       // per-AIR pointer array on device\n66\t    const FpExt *eq_cube;              // [num_x]\n67\t    const Fp *public_values;           // per-AIR\n68\t    const Rule *d_rules;               // per-AIR constraint DAG\n69\t    const size_t *d_used_nodes;        // per-AIR used node indices\n70\t    size_t rules_len;\n71\t    size_t used_nodes_len;\n72\t    uint32_t buffer_size;              // must be <= BUFFER_THRESHOLD for batching\n73\t    uint32_t num_x;                    // 1 << n_lift\n74\t    uint32_t height;                   // trace height\n75\t    uint32_t num_cosets;               // constraint_degree - 1\n76\t    Fp g_shift;                        // omega_root for this AIR\n77\t};\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t**File: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`**\n81\t\n82\tAdd in the `logup_round0` namespace:\n83\t\n84\t```cpp\n85\tstruct LogupBatchMeta {\n86\t    const Fp *selectors_cube;\n87\t    const Fp *preprocessed;\n88\t    const Fp *const *main_parts;\n89\t    const FpExt *eq_cube;\n90\t    const Fp *public_values;\n91\t    const FpExt *numer_weights;        // per-AIR, freshly computed\n92\t    const FpExt *denom_weights;        // per-AIR, freshly computed\n93\t    const Rule *d_rules;               // per-AIR, freshly compiled DAG\n94\t    size_t rules_len;\n95\t    FpExt denom_sum_init;              // per-AIR scalar\n96\t    uint32_t buffer_size;              // must be <= BUFFER_THRESHOLD for batching\n97\t    uint32_t num_x;\n98\t    uint32_t height;\n99\t    uint32_t num_cosets;               // constraint_degree\n100\t    Fp g_shift;\n101\t};\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\t### Change 2: CUDA — Batched evaluation kernels\n105\t\n106\t**File: `zerocheck_round0.cu`**\n107\t\n108\tAdd `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_batched_kernel<NEEDS_SHMEM>`:\n109\t\n110\t- **Grid**: `(total_x_blocks, max_num_cosets)` — `total_x_blocks` = sum of per-AIR `ceil(num_x * skip_domain / blockDim.x)` across all batched AIRs\n111\t- **Block**: `(MAX_THREADS=128, 1, 1)` — uniform for all blocks\n112\t- **Template**: `GLOBAL=false` only (local intermediates). `NEEDS_SHMEM` dispatched at runtime based on `skip_domain > WARP_SIZE`\n113\t- **Additional kernel parameters** (beyond the per-AIR metadata):\n114\t  - `const ZerocheckBatchMeta *air_metas` — [num_airs] on device\n115\t  - `const uint32_t *air_for_block` — [total_x_blocks] maps each blockIdx.x to an AIR index\n116\t  - `const uint32_t *segment_offsets` — [num_airs + 1] cumulative x_blocks per AIR\n117\t  - `const FpExt *d_lambda_pows` — shared across all AIRs\n118\t  - `size_t lambda_len` — shared\n119\t  - `uint32_t skip_domain` — shared (constant across all AIRs)\n120\t  - `uint32_t d` — output stride = `max_num_cosets * skip_domain`\n121\t\n122\t**Kernel body (derived from existing coset_parallel kernel at lines 335-467):**\n123\t\n124\t1. Load AIR identity: `air_idx = air_for_block[blockIdx.x]`, `meta = air_metas[air_idx]`\n125\t2. Compute local block position: `local_block_x = blockIdx.x - segment_offsets[air_idx]`\n126\t3. Extract coset: `coset_idx = blockIdx.y`\n127\t4. **Bounds check**: if `coset_idx >= meta.num_cosets`, return early (pre-zeroed buffer handles the padding)\n128\t5. Compute thread indexing using `local_block_x` and `meta.num_x`:\n129\t   - `tidx = threadIdx.x + local_block_x * blockDim.x`\n130\t   - `ntt_idx = tidx & (skip_domain - 1)`\n131\t   - `x_int_base = tidx >> l_skip`\n132\t   - `air_x_blocks = div_ceil(meta.num_x * skip_domain, blockDim.x)`\n133\t   - `x_int_stride = (air_x_blocks * blockDim.x) >> l_skip`\n134\t6. Precompute coset values using `meta.g_shift`, `coset_idx` — identical to existing kernel lines 387-393\n135\t7. Set up `NttEvalContext<1>` using `meta.*` fields — identical to existing lines 414-426\n136\t8. Main loop over `x_int` — identical to existing lines 428-448, using `meta.*` for selectors/rules\n137\t9. **Zerofier division and in-block reduction** — identical to existing lines 450-466:\n138\t   - Compute `eval_point = g_coset * omega_skip_ntt` where `g_coset = pow(meta.g_shift, coset_idx + 1)` (per-AIR g_shift from metadata)\n139\t   - Compute `zerofier = exp_power_of_2(eval_point, l_skip) - Fp::one()`\n140\t   - Write `shared_sum[threadIdx.x] = sum * inv(zerofier)`, then block-reduce across lanes\n141\t   - The zerofier is never zero because `g_shift` is not in the skip domain and we use `(coset_idx + 1)` power\n142\t10. **Output**: `tmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * d + coset_idx * skip_domain + ntt_idx] = tile_sum`\n143\t    - Uses global `blockIdx.x` (not local_block_x) so blocks from different AIRs write to non-overlapping regions\n144\t\n145\t**File: `logup_round0.cu`**\n146\t\n147\tAdd `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_batched_kernel<NEEDS_SHMEM>`:\n148\t\n149\tSame structure as zerocheck batched kernel, with these differences:\n150\t- Uses `FracExt` output type (shared_sum is `FracExt *`)\n151\t- Calls `acc_interactions<1, NEEDS_SHMEM, false>` with `is_identity_coset = (coset_idx == 0)` as `skip_ntt` flag — identical to existing lines 425-437\n152\t- Per-AIR data includes `meta.numer_weights`, `meta.denom_weights`, `meta.denom_sum_init`\n153\t- Shared memory: `sizeof(FracExt) * blockDim.x + (NEEDS_SHMEM ? sizeof(Fp) * blockDim.x : 0)`\n154\t- Output: `tmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * d + coset_idx * skip_domain + ntt_idx] = tile_sum` where `tile_sum` is `FracExt`\n155\t\n156\t### Change 3: CUDA — Batched launcher functions (extern \"C\")\n157\t\n158\t**File: `zerocheck_round0.cu`**\n159\t\n160\tAdd launcher that combines evaluation kernel + batched reduction:\n161\t\n162\t```cpp\n163\textern \"C\" int _zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched(\n164\t    FpExt *tmp_sums_buffer,                  // pre-zeroed, [total_x_blocks][d]\n165\t    FpExt *output,                           // [num_airs][d]\n166\t    const ZerocheckBatchMeta *metas,         // [num_airs], device\n167\t    const uint32_t *air_for_block,           // [total_x_blocks], device\n168\t    const uint32_t *segment_offsets,         // [num_airs + 1], device\n169\t    const FpExt *d_lambda_pows,              // shared\n170\t    size_t lambda_len,\n171\t    uint32_t num_airs,\n172\t    uint32_t total_x_blocks,\n173\t    uint32_t max_num_cosets,\n174\t    uint32_t skip_domain\n175\t);\n176\t```\n177\t\n178\tLogic:\n179\t1. `d = max_num_cosets * skip_domain`\n180\t2. `grid = dim3(total_x_blocks, max_num_cosets)`, `block = dim3(MAX_THREADS)`\n181\t3. Compute shmem: `sizeof(FpExt) * block.x + (needs_shmem ? sizeof(Fp) * block.x : 0)`\n182\t4. Dispatch on `needs_shmem = skip_domain > WARP_SIZE`: launch batched evaluation kernel\n183\t5. Launch `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` (from sumcheck.cuh:261-291):\n184\t   - `reduce_grid = dim3(num_airs, d)`, `reduce_block` from `kernel_launch_params(max_blocks_per_segment)`\n185\t     where `max_blocks_per_segment` = max over all AIRs of their x_blocks count\n186\t   - `reduce_shmem = div_ceil(reduce_block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt)`\n187\t   - Parameters: `tmp_sums_buffer, output, segment_offsets, d`\n188\t\n189\t**File: `logup_round0.cu`**\n190\t\n191\tAdd analogous launcher:\n192\t\n193\t```cpp\n194\textern \"C\" int _logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched(\n195\t    FracExt *tmp_sums_buffer,                // pre-zeroed, [total_x_blocks][d_frac]\n196\t    FracExt *output,                         // [num_airs][d_frac]\n197\t    const LogupBatchMeta *metas,             // [num_airs], device\n198\t    const uint32_t *air_for_block,           // [total_x_blocks], device\n199\t    const uint32_t *segment_offsets,         // [num_airs + 1], device\n200\t    uint32_t num_airs,\n201\t    uint32_t total_x_blocks,\n202\t    uint32_t max_num_cosets,\n203\t    uint32_t skip_domain\n204\t);\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\tSame pattern. For the reduction, reinterpret `FracExt` as `FpExt` (2 components):\n208\t- `d_fpext = 2 * max_num_cosets * skip_domain`\n209\t- Launch `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` with `dim3(num_airs, d_fpext)` and `d = d_fpext`\n210\t\n211\t### Change 4: Rust FFI declarations\n212\t\n213\t**File: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`**\n214\t\n215\tAdd to the `extern \"C\"` block:\n216\t\n217\t```rust\n218\tfn _zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched(\n219\t    tmp_sums_buffer: *mut EF,\n220\t    output: *mut EF,\n221\t    metas: *const std::ffi::c_void,    // ZerocheckBatchMeta*\n222\t    air_for_block: *const u32,\n223\t    segment_offsets: *const u32,\n224\t    d_lambda_pows: *const EF,\n225\t    lambda_len: usize,\n226\t    num_airs: u32,\n227\t    total_x_blocks: u32,\n228\t    max_num_cosets: u32,\n229\t    skip_domain: u32,\n230\t) -> i32;\n231\t\n232\tfn _logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched(\n233\t    tmp_sums_buffer: *mut Frac<EF>,\n234\t    output: *mut Frac<EF>,\n235\t    metas: *const std::ffi::c_void,    // LogupBatchMeta*\n236\t    air_for_block: *const u32,\n237\t    segment_offsets: *const u32,\n238\t    num_airs: u32,\n239\t    total_x_blocks: u32,\n240\t    max_num_cosets: u32,\n241\t    skip_domain: u32,\n242\t) -> i32;\n243\t```\n244\t\n245\tAdd safe Rust wrapper functions following the existing pattern (see `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints` at lines 924-967).\n246\t\n247\t### Change 5: Rust metadata structs\n248\t\n249\t**File: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`**\n250\t\n251\tAdd `#[repr(C)]` structs matching the CUDA definitions exactly (same field order and types):\n252\t\n253\t```rust\n254\t#[repr(C)]\n255\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n256\tpub(crate) struct ZerocheckBatchMeta {\n257\t    pub selectors_cube: *const F,\n258\t    pub preprocessed: *const F,\n259\t    pub main_parts: *const *const F,\n260\t    pub eq_cube: *const EF,\n261\t    pub public_values: *const F,\n262\t    pub d_rules: *const std::ffi::c_void,   // Rule*\n263\t    pub d_used_nodes: *const usize,\n264\t    pub rules_len: usize,\n265\t    pub used_nodes_len: usize,\n266\t    pub buffer_size: u32,\n267\t    pub num_x: u32,\n268\t    pub height: u32,\n269\t    pub num_cosets: u32,\n270\t    pub g_shift: F,\n271\t}\n272\t\n273\t#[repr(C)]\n274\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n275\tpub(crate) struct LogupBatchMeta {\n276\t    pub selectors_cube: *const F,\n277\t    pub preprocessed: *const F,\n278\t    pub main_parts: *const *const F,\n279\t    pub eq_cube: *const EF,\n280\t    pub public_values: *const F,\n281\t    pub numer_weights: *const EF,\n282\t    pub denom_weights: *const EF,\n283\t    pub d_rules: *const std::ffi::c_void,\n284\t    pub rules_len: usize,\n285\t    pub denom_sum_init: EF,\n286\t    pub buffer_size: u32,\n287\t    pub num_x: u32,\n288\t    pub height: u32,\n289\t    pub num_cosets: u32,\n290\t    pub g_shift: F,\n291\t}\n292\t```\n293\t\n294\tBoth structs must be `unsafe impl Send` (contains raw pointers to device memory).\n295\t\n296\t### Change 6: Rust orchestration\n297\t\n298\t**File: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`**\n299\t\n300\tModify `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` Phase 1 (lines 744-841). Replace the single per-AIR loop with three sub-phases:\n301\t\n302\t#### Sub-phase A: Classify AIRs and collect metadata\n303\t\n304\tIterate all AIR instances (same loop structure as current lines 750-757). For each AIR:\n305\t\n306\t1. Compute `num_x = 1 << n_lift`, `skip_domain = 1 << l_skip`\n307\t2. Check `is_coset_parallel = (num_x * skip_domain) < 32768`\n308\t3. Build `d_main_parts` (same as current lines 781-786). Store in a keep-alive vec.\n309\t\n310\t**For zerocheck:**\n311\t4. Check `num_cosets_zc > 0` and has constraints (same as `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` early-return checks)\n312\t5. Read `buffer_size = pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0.inner.buffer_size`\n313\t6. Check `batch_eligible_zc = is_coset_parallel && buffer_size <= 16`\n314\t7. If eligible: build `ZerocheckBatchMeta` from existing device data (pk fields, selectors, eq_cube, etc.)\n315\t   - Compute `x_blocks = ceil(num_x * skip_domain / 128)`\n316\t   - Add to `zc_batch_metas` vec, record `x_blocks`\n317\t8. If not eligible: mark for individual launch\n318\t\n319\t**For logup:**\n320\t9. Check `!eq_3bs.is_empty()` (has interactions)\n321\t10. Perform the per-AIR CPU work: build symbolic DAG, compute weights, compile rules (lines 161-207 of round0.rs)\n322\t11. Upload `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` to device. Store in keep-alive vecs.\n323\t12. Read `buffer_size` from compiled rules\n324\t13. Check `batch_eligible_logup = is_coset_parallel && buffer_size <= 16`\n325\t14. If eligible: build `LogupBatchMeta` with device pointers from step 11\n326\t    - Compute `x_blocks`, add to `logup_batch_metas` vec\n327\t15. If not eligible: mark for individual launch\n328\t\n329\tCompute for each batch:\n330\t- `total_x_blocks` = sum of per-AIR x_blocks\n331\t- `max_num_cosets` = max of per-AIR num_cosets\n332\t- `segment_offsets` = prefix sum of per-AIR x_blocks (length num_airs + 1)\n333\t- `air_for_block` = flat mapping, e.g., if AIR 0 has 3 blocks and AIR 1 has 2 blocks: `[0, 0, 0, 1, 1]`\n334\t\n335\t#### Sub-phase B: Batched launches\n336\t\n337\t**Zerocheck batch** (if `zc_batch_metas` non-empty):\n338\t1. Upload `zc_batch_metas`, `air_for_block`, `segment_offsets` to device\n339\t2. Allocate `d_zc_tmp` with capacity `total_x_blocks * d` (where `d = max_num_cosets * skip_domain`), zero-initialize via `fill_zero()`\n340\t3. Allocate `d_zc_output` with capacity `num_airs * d`\n341\t4. Call `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched(d_zc_tmp, d_zc_output, ...)`\n342\t\n343\t**Logup batch** (if `logup_batch_metas` non-empty):\n344\t1. Upload `logup_batch_metas`, mapping arrays to device\n345\t2. Allocate `d_logup_tmp` with capacity `total_x_blocks * d_logup` (where `d_logup = max_num_cosets_logup * skip_domain`), zero-initialize\n346\t3. Allocate `d_logup_output` with capacity `num_airs_logup * d_logup`\n347\t4. Call `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched(d_logup_tmp, d_logup_output, ...)`\n348\t\n349\t#### Sub-phase C: Individual launches\n350\t\n351\tFor non-batch-eligible AIRs, call existing `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and/or `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` as before.\n352\t\n353\t#### Phase 2 modifications\n354\t\n355\tAfter `current_stream_sync()`:\n356\t1. D2H the batched output buffers (`d_zc_output.to_host()`, `d_logup_output.to_host()`)\n357\t2. Drop keep-alive vecs (per-AIR logup DeviceBuffers, d_main_parts)\n358\t3. For each batched AIR, extract its slice from the flat output:\n359\t   - Zerocheck: `&zc_host_output[batch_idx * d .. batch_idx * d + actual_num_cosets * skip_domain]`\n360\t   - Logup: `&logup_host_output[batch_idx * d_logup .. batch_idx * d_logup + actual_num_cosets_logup * skip_domain]`\n361\t4. Feed into existing polynomial construction (lines 850-923) — **this code is unchanged**\n362\t5. Individual-launch AIR results handled via existing `Round0Pending` path\n363\t\n364\t### Design decisions\n365\t\n366\t1. **2D grid vs 3D grid**: Using 2D grid `(total_x_blocks, max_num_cosets)` with flat `air_for_block` mapping. A 3D grid `(max_x_blocks, max_num_cosets, num_airs)` would waste blocks when AIRs have varying x_block counts (e.g., 256 max_x_blocks but most AIRs have 1-2 → 98%+ blocks return early).\n367\t\n368\t2. **GLOBAL=false only**: Only batching AIRs with `buffer_size <= BUFFER_THRESHOLD (16)`. The GLOBAL=true path requires per-AIR global intermediate buffers whose aggregate size could be significant (~73 MB for 500 AIRs). GLOBAL=true AIRs continue with individual launches. This captures the majority of small AIRs (large DAGs requiring buffer_size > 16 are uncommon for small traces).\n369\t\n370\t3. **Uniform blockDim.x = 128**: All batched blocks use MAX_THREADS. AIRs with fewer threads (small num_x) have idle threads that contribute zero in the reduction. The cost is negligible — these idle threads' shared_sum writes are zero and don't affect correctness.\n371\t\n372\t4. **Pre-zeroed tmp_sums_buffer**: Blocks with `coset_idx >= meta.num_cosets` return early without writing. Zero-initialization ensures the reduction reads zeros for padding positions. Cost: < 0.1ms for ~200 KB.\n373\t\n374\t5. **Reuse `batched_final_reduce_block_sums`**: Available in `sumcheck.cuh:261-291`. Already supports segment offsets for multi-segment reduction. Currently unused but compiled — will be exercised by this change.\n375\t\n376\t6. **Separate zerocheck and logup batches**: Different kernel logic (constraint accumulation vs interaction numerator/denominator), different output types (`FpExt` vs `FracExt`), and different per-AIR data preparation (pre-built rules vs per-AIR DAG compilation).\n377\t\n378\t7. **Per-AIR logup CPU work unchanged**: DAG compilation, weight computation, and per-AIR H2D uploads still happen sequentially per AIR. The optimization targets GPU execution time (sequential kernel launches → concurrent), not CPU-side preparation. Note: if the batched kernel reduces GPU time by 3-5x, the sequential CPU preparation (~396 AIRs worth of DAG building and weight computation) could become visible in the profile. If so, rayon-parallelizing the logup CPU preparation is a natural follow-up.\n379\t\n380\t8. **Sub-batching by `num_cosets` as follow-up**: The current plan uses `max_num_cosets` for the grid's y-dimension, causing AIRs with fewer cosets to waste coset-dimension blocks (early-return). If profiling shows this waste is significant (e.g., `max_num_cosets = 4` but most AIRs have `num_cosets = 2`), grouping AIRs by identical `num_cosets` into separate sub-batches would eliminate the padding. This adds at most 2-3 extra launches (one per distinct `num_cosets` value) while simplifying the kernel (no per-AIR coset bounds check). Deferring this to a follow-up since the waste factor is at most 2-3x on the coset dimension, which is small relative to the 30-100x improvement from batching the x-block dimension.\n381\t\n382\t## Invariants\n383\t\n384\t1. **Per-AIR output values are bit-identical** to the current non-batched code. The batched kernel executes the same arithmetic per (AIR, coset, x_int, ntt_idx) as the existing coset-parallel kernel. Only the launch geometry and reduction strategy differ.\n385\t\n386\t2. **Non-coset-parallel AIRs are completely unaffected**. They continue using the existing per-AIR lockstep kernel path.\n387\t\n388\t3. **Phase 2 polynomial construction is unchanged**. It receives the same per-AIR `q_evals` / `s_evals` arrays regardless of whether they came from batched or individual launches.\n389\t\n390\t4. **Memory safety**: All per-AIR DeviceBuffers referenced by metadata pointers are kept alive until after stream sync. The VPMM's stream-ordered deallocation ensures device memory is valid during kernel execution.\n391\t\n392\t5. **COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD is unchanged** (32768). The same AIRs that currently use coset-parallel mode will be batched.\n393\t\n394\t6. **BUFFER_THRESHOLD is unchanged** (16). AIRs with buffer_size > 16 continue using individual launches with global intermediates.\n395\t\n396\t## Measurement Plan\n397\t\n398\t### Correctness verification\n399\t\n400\t1. Run the full test suite:\n401\t   ```bash\n402\t   cargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4\n403\t   ```\n404\t   All 94 tests must pass.\n405\t\n406\t2. Run pairing benchmark for APC {0, 100, 300} using the powdr repo:\n407\t   ```bash\n408\t   openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh\n409\t   ```\n410\t   Proof verification must succeed for all configurations.\n411\t\n412\t### Performance measurement\n413\t\n414\t1. Collect metrics for APC {0, 100, 300}:\n415\t   - Before: use latest `autoopt-results/2026-04-10-2145-batch-degenerate-stacked-reduction/results/` as baseline\n416\t   - After: run pairing for each APC config\n417\t\n418\t2. Analyze with `spec.py`:\n419\t   ```\n420\t   python spec.py <metrics_json> <experiment_name>\n421\t   ```\n422\t   Compare \"Round 0\" and \"STARK (excl. trace)\" across APC configurations.\n423\t\n424\t3. Use Nsight Systems to verify GPU utilization improvement:\n425\t   ```bash\n426\t   nsys profile --stats=true <command>\n427\t   ```\n428\t   Check that the ~935 individual `coset_parallel` kernel launches are replaced by 2 batched launches + 2 batched reductions.\n429\t\n430\t### Diagnostic: batch coverage\n431\t\n432\tAdd a temporary `debug!` log line counting how many AIRs are batch-eligible vs individual for zerocheck and logup at each APC config. Expected: >90% of coset-parallel AIRs are batch-eligible (GLOBAL=false). If <70% are eligible, consider adding GLOBAL=true batching as a follow-up.\n433\t\n434\t## Rollback Criteria\n435\t\n436\t1. **Any test failure**: Revert immediately. The batched kernel must produce bit-identical results.\n437\t2. **Round 0 APC 300 > 500ms**: Less than 12% improvement doesn't justify the added code complexity. Investigate whether GLOBAL=true AIRs dominate and consider adding that path.\n438\t3. **STARK excl trace APC 300 regression for APC 0**: The optimization should be neutral or positive for APC 0 (few small AIRs). Any regression indicates a bug.\n439\t4. **Peak GPU memory increase > 100 MB**: The batched buffers should total < 5 MB. Significant memory increase indicates a sizing error.\n440\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NuzYvE5zkA1q9Vs1qoXDoc","session_id":"db10821c-17ee-4d4a-acd4-fd3a20fcece6","uuid":"478cedf0-fedb-4fbb-a311-9bea82eb84d8","timestamp":"2026-04-10T19:15:55.545Z"}
